Chapter: Sensors

 The Sensors effect is the right to read the machine's inertial and
 environmental sensors. It is a bare marker here, the way Microphone and
 Location are: accelerometer, gyroscope, barometer and light-level are
 not declared in this chapter.

 They were, once, with the same defect Location had. Four effect
 operations with no handler anywhere meant every one of them
 type-checked clean and died at emit with CDX2040. Two of them answered
 `Pair Integer (Pair Integer Integer)` while this chapter cited nothing
 at all, so the name never resolved to Foreword chapter Pair and never
 had to: a declaration nothing can call is never asked what it means.
 SensorsStub answers with a named three-axis record instead, because
 nesting pairs to carry x, y and z is a tuple wearing a disguise.

 This machine has no accelerometer, no gyroscope, no barometer and no
 ambient light sensor. A chapter that wants the operations anyway cites
 Foreword chapter SensorsStub and gets constants; a chapter that does
 not gets CDX3002 on the name.

 We say:

Section: Definitions

  effect Sensors where

